course: dictionary
lesson: 4241
title: Grandparents and family words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A grandparent is a parent of your mum or your dad: your grandma or your grandad. «Old card and board games from grandparents' childhoods are still fun to play today.» The words grandparents' childhoods tell you that grandparents were children long ago, so their games are old.
explain: Grandparents is the plural, so it means two or more grandparents together. Each person usually has four grandparents: two on the mum's side and two on the dad's side. Mum's side is a useful phrase when you talk about your family.
explain: «Grandparents carry family history that only they can tell.» The clue is family history: a grandparent can tell you stories about your family from long ago. Grandma, gran, nan, granny, grandpa, grandad and pop are all words people use for grandparents.
fact: A grandparent is the parent of your mother or father.
fact: Grandparents is the plural: it means two or more grandparents together.
fact: Most people have four grandparents.
fact: «Grandad» and «nan» are everyday words for grandparents.
fact: A great-grandparent is one step further up the family tree: the parent of a grandparent.
exercise: What is a grandparent? | A cousin who lives far away | A child in your class | *A parent of your mum or dad | A teacher at your school
exercise: Which word means two or more grandparents together? | Grandad | *Grandparents | Grandparent | Grandma
exercise: «Old card and board games from grandparents' childhoods are still fun to play today.» What do the words grandparents' childhoods mean? | Their grandchildren's birthdays | The games they played yesterday | Their homes | *The time when the grandparents were children
test: Your mum's dad is your | Cousin | *Grandad | Brother
test: How many grandparents does most people have? | *Four | Two | Ten | Six
exam: Which is the best meaning of a great-grandparent? | A teacher who tells family stories | A cousin of your mum | *The parent of a grandparent | A child who lives next door
